185
00:24:14,711 --> 00:24:21,991
Then I can create orange button class and green button class by using inheritance, for example.

186
00:24:22,451 --> 00:24:25,231
Or let's say red, yellow and purple, for example.

187
00:24:26,152 --> 00:24:30,211
Instead of doing this, you can do much better modeling.

188
00:24:30,372 --> 00:24:30,591
Why?

189
00:24:31,188 --> 00:24:38,847
Because that customer wants those particular three colors and other customers will want many different colors.

190
00:24:40,008 --> 00:24:48,367
When you try to create a new class for every desired color, soon you will have hundreds of classes.

191
00:24:49,508 --> 00:24:54,607
And it will be very hard to maintain those classes.

192
00:24:55,124 --> 00:25:10,283
Let's suppose that you have a bug in the GUI-BATTLE class, then you have to collect those bugs in every subclass, which is a maintenance nightmare.

193
00:25:11,283 --> 00:25:18,083
You can do better. How? Please consider what actually changes.

194
00:25:18,771 --> 00:25:23,151
What actually changes is the color of the button.

195
00:25:24,051 --> 00:25:33,231
Well, in that case, every button will have a color, which means association, ownership association.

196
00:25:34,231 --> 00:25:38,311
The color is changing, so create a color class.

197
00:25:41,715 --> 00:25:49,315
And when trying to generate a color, there are three main colors, red, green and blue.

198
00:25:49,315 --> 00:26:05,235
And by giving those three main colors intensities between 0 and 255, you can create 16 million colors.

199
00:26:06,996 --> 00:26:16,916
Create a RGB class, or let's, or you can name it color or anything you wish, and have three members here, red, green, and blue.

200
00:26:17,616 --> 00:26:29,612
And when painting a button, drawing a button to the screen or a platform, etc., in the body of that print method, first...

201
00:26:29,683 --> 00:26:33,084
Take a paintbrush from the system.

202
00:26:33,744 --> 00:26:37,703
Every operating system and framework has such statements.

203
00:26:37,884 --> 00:26:44,703
You give red, green, and blue values between 0 and 265.

204
00:26:45,324 --> 00:26:49,344
Then the system gives you the appropriate color.

205
00:26:49,963 --> 00:26:55,443
And when you draw or paint something, then they will be drawn by using that color.

206
00:26:56,019 --> 00:27:07,799
Therefore, please create this RGB class and obtain one-to-one ownership association between the button class and that RGB class.

207
00:27:08,360 --> 00:27:10,059
This is the correct modeling.

208
00:27:10,720 --> 00:27:14,880
The one on the left is the incorrect use of inheritance.

